// Regression: the generated main wrapper used to call the runtime async wait
// unconditionally after the entry function returned. The yak VM has no such
// implicit wait — it returns as soon as the main flow ends and leaves
// background goroutines running; that is exactly why waitAllAsyncCallFinish()
// exists. The unconditional wait deadlocked every "start a server, drive it,
// return" script, whose serve loop never finishes on its own (mitm_*,
// http_lowhttp, head_chunked_test, ...), turning them into 90s timeouts.
//
// This script leaves a goroutine sleeping far longer than the process should
// live, so the test only passes if the wrapper really does not wait.
go func {
    time.sleep(600)
}
println("main flow finished")
